__There seems to be currently some bugs in share-link to json config conversion logic of v2rayN, causing perfectly valid share links to return -1 on connectivity testing__ (even using the latest 7.21.3 built).

My partial chat with copilot regarding this repo and this specific issue: 

>...Why It Fails with Non-Default Settings
> 
>     Default settings: When User Agent is the default (empty/null), line 523's condition if (useragent.IsNotEmpty()) is false, so line 525 never executes. The settings object gets serialized with a missing headers block—which works because it serializes to null.
> 
>     Custom settings: When you set a custom User Agent in Settings > Core, useragent contains a value, triggering line 525. Attempting to access .headers.UserAgent on a null headers object causes an exception or fails silently, leaving httpupgradeSettings incomplete.
> 
> The Fix
> 
> The code should initialize headers just like wsSettings does at line 494:
> 
> ...
> 
> This is a regression test gap—the existing FmtHandlerTests only tests with default settings and simple profiles, never testing with modified app settings like custom User Agent or TLS fingerprints applied during config generation.



### Reproduction method 

Change some settings (specially under Settings > Core) from default to non default ones and then paste this share link `vless://00000000-aaaa-bbbb-cccc-dddddddddddd@xxxxx.com:443?type=httpupgrade&encryption=none&path=%2Fforum&host=&security=tls&fp=firefox&alpn=h3%2Ch2%2Chttp%2F1.1&sni=xxxxx.com#TEST`  and see that the expanded json confg does not include the `httpupgradeSettings` block!

### 相关问题

ShouldApplySendThrough currently ignores the freedom (direct) protocol, so sendThrough does not apply. I suggest changing the condition to allow direct connections to use interface binding.

### 描述你希望的解决方案

Change the condition in `ShouldApplySendThrough` from:

```csharp
if (outbound.protocol is "freedom" or "blackhole" or "dns" or "loopback")
{
    return false;
}
```

to:

```csharp
if (outbound.protocol is "blackhole" or "dns" or "loopback")
{
    return false;
}
```

This allows `freedom` (direct) connections to use `sendThrough` for interface binding.

